A||||11||prof bobo||Openable rear window - any ideas?||||1||
Z||000000||prof bobo||08-21-2000||07:08 PM||||I'd like to replace my rear window with something that opens, tilt in/out O.K., slide open (like the ones in a pick-up) better,  removeable, ideal.  <P>Anybody seen or know of any kit to do this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||08-21-2000||07:21 PM||||Check out V8 Archie, His chop top fiero's have removeable Lexan rear windows, I think I read that on his site Idon't know if he makes them regular size. <P>V8ARCHIE.COM||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||08-21-2000||08:40 PM||||Here's what I'd do:<BR> Go to the auto parts store and buy a new rear slider for a mini truck (s-10?) for $75. Remove the glass and cut the frame down to fit the fiero window opening. Take the new frame and hardware to a glass shop and have them fit it with new glass. If you use lexan you could cut it yourself. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||08-21-2000||08:46 PM||||Nice idea, kind of like the del sol. But remember that the engine with all its noise and heat is right there.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||08-21-2000||11:47 PM||||This has been discussed several times with a fair amount of good info. Try running a search, not sure what to search for though. I would be concerned mostly about engine cooling(the notchback isn't there for looks alone), engine noise, and engine heat on your neck.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||08-22-2000||11:03 AM||||Ya know, it would be kind of interesting to open the window in the middle of winter for some extra heat in the cabin tho...||||reg||12
Z||000006||theogre||08-22-2000||01:15 PM||||The other thing to worry about with this is pulling in exhaust fumes. Almost no exhaust is 100% leak free.||||reg||1
Z||000007||85SE||08-23-2000||03:54 PM||||I also thought that the rear window was part of the structural integrity of the car?  At least, I think that's what Ed Parks has said - they don't even remove the rear windows at The Fiero Factory due to the forces at play with the rear window.  Archie, got your ears on?  Curious as to your thoughts as a tuner.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||08-23-2000||04:00 PM||||You will get all kinds of exhaust heat and fumes.  If you have a sunroof, just crack it open and stick your fingers out while you're driving.. I know on mine that the air right there is pretty warm..  Or just feel the rear glass after you've been driving for a bit..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||HugGRRRFiero||08-23-2000||04:15 PM||||85SE, yes I've heard the windows in a car do play a part in the structural integrity of a car.  <P>Now why in the world would you want to have a rear opening window?  So you could roast hotdogs on the vented decks while driving around?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Mine had an aftermarket sunroof (RV port hole looking thing) when I bought it.  I drove around once with it open and it sucked the heat right in from the deck.  I'm not big on sunroofs and it had to go anyway so I replaced it with a hardtop.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 08-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||the need for speed||08-24-2000||04:00 AM||||I think this is a great idea to try out,kind of like a convertible or a motorcycle feeling having the air rush past you, and also taking heat out the rear of the car.I saw that archie did it on the chop top fiero i asked if he sells a kit, he said it was around $400. You will probable have to go with the lexan window, probable lighter to. I think archie said when you remove it, that it fits in the trunk for easy carry along.I didn't see any thing on this mod when i did a search. Can you post if you do this mod thanks||||reg||14
Z||000011||Philphine||08-24-2000||10:21 AM||||vette coupes from '68 to about '72 had this. i've been keeping a half eye out for one for my '74. don't know any thing about it since i've never really seen one. maybe if you know someone with one of those years you can get a look at it and see how well the idea would transfer. now that i think about it, i guess i could measure both back windows and see how close in size they are.<P>do convertible owners have heat problems like you all are describing? i'd still like to take the top off a fiero if i can.||||reg||1
